/*  EXPECTED: COMPILES and runs; compiled output must match the interpreter.

    A method sets a field of the object it is cast on to the text it is given. Cast inside a rabbit,
    with a text made there, on an object from outside it (the probe `param-5`).

    A text is never refused; one stored where a body cannot see how long the target lives is
    copied, when the program runs, into the region the target itself lives in (docs/SOUNDNESS.md,
    obligation O4). */

Define object box with (the text tag).
Bind void to retag unto box, given (the text t):
    One's tag becomes t.
Done.
Define keeper as a new box { the tag "outer" }.
Pull a rabbit.
    Cast keeper's retag on ("in" joined to "ner").
Done.

Define churn as a series of text.
Define tick as 0.
While tick is less than 400, repeat:
    Insert ("zzzzzzzz" joined to "yyyyyyyy") into churn.
    tick becomes tick + 1.
Done.
State keeper's tag.
